  "body": "Eight sampled operations display the same source-search fallback, including machinery jobs, and ARRIVALS does not explain its count. This change displays operation-aware STATUS wording from public state and explains received signals, including zero. Simulation messages and context remain unchanged.\n\nActual baseline touch checks also exposed off-screen command controls and Back on the cover viewport. A reversible adapter fits the existing full-size radial controls and scrollable sheets to the viewport, retaining command order, buttons and touch handling. No simulation, operation-table, save or sensing rules change. Table.enabled=false restores prior presentation; Layout.enabled=false restores prior geometry, including its existing clipping.\n\nBase: e0ee34d356d61c42e9809305647415c103e3cf84. Head: e1dbc026b851d13bf50d6d01abe2d4e60395d379.\n\nLocal development checks passed: import; core 836; wording 74; headless UI 1,208; native UI 1,412 with 28 captures; unchanged affected suites 343. Independent nonauthor review passed the same 3,873 assertions plus an external refresh/resize/hit-mapping probe with 764 checks. All reported passing checks have zero failures. Original failed development and reviewer probes are preserved. Review provenance and limitations: https://github.com/pemunson90-cmd/Siren-s-Song/pull/146#issuecomment-6405622605 . Full local scenario matrix was not run.\n\nGuidance now indexes the module, tests and reverts, corrects the 048/050 boundary, and records Pat's research/reuse instruction. Official Godot 4.6 Control and Container references were checked: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.6/classes/class_control.html and https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.6/tutorials/ui/gui_containers.html . Existing controls, input helpers and scroll containers are reused; the custom drawn command ring needs a bounded geometry adapter.\n\nFinal hosted run 40249328277: guidance passed; game-smoke pending. This is technical desktop evidence, not full-campaign, blind-player or physical-phone acceptance. Sight-only Hunt 050 is not implemented here.",
